OVERVIEW: Hexadecimal dump with DICOM structure visualization

Displays hexadecimal dump of DICOM files with structure annotations.
Useful for low-level debugging and format inspection.

Examples:
  dicom-dump file.dcm
  dicom-dump file.dcm --tag 7FE0,0010
  dicom-dump file.dcm --tag PatientName --verbose
  dicom-dump file.dcm --offset 0x1000 --length 256
  dicom-dump file.dcm --no-color > dump.txt

USAGE: dicom-dump <file-path> [--tag <tag>] [--offset <offset>] [--length <length>] [--bytes-per-line <bytes-per-line>] [--highlight <highlight>] [--no-color] [--annotate] [--force] [--verbose]

ARGUMENTS:
  <file-path>             Path to DICOM file

OPTIONS:
  --tag <tag>             Dump specific tag (format: 0010,0010 or PS3.6
                          keyword, e.g. PatientName)
  --offset <offset>       Start offset in bytes (hex or decimal)
  --length <length>       Number of bytes to dump
  --bytes-per-line <bytes-per-line>
                          Bytes per line (default: 16) (default: 16)
  --highlight <highlight> Highlight specific tag (format: 0010,0010 or PS3.6
                          keyword)
  --no-color              Disable color output
  --annotate              Show tag annotations
  --force                 Force parsing of files without DICM prefix
  --verbose               Verbose output with VR and length details
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

